    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0191" n="149" xml:id="pg149"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 338.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-02-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 27, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I now transmit the copy of a note addressed
                    to me by Lord Russell, in answer to mine of the 19th instant, a copy of which
                    was forwarded last week with my despatch (No. 328) of the same date. I believe
                    this is the first instance of a censure by the government here of any act done
                    by its subordinates during the present struggle. In the mean time, however, the
                    Gladiator is announced as just arrived at Liverpool with half a million of the
                    money.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d96-a1.xml" xpointer="d96-a1"/>
            </div>
